      "message": "fix(multiaxis): prove Rotary Flow sweeps, keep closed laps, read width at every knot\n\nReview round on PR #3630 (all seven items of the pr-reviewer comment):\n\n- Every emitted move (flow chords, plunges, retracts, links, exit) is\n  proved clear as a swept ball by the exact segment-to-triangle\n  distance, with the interpolated-axis drift added. Stations are pushed\n  out to r + tol; a chord is accepted only when its sweep keeps\n  r + tol/2, else bisected; at the depth cap an unproved chord refuses.\n  The final guard refuses the program at the first unproved move.\n- A closed guide keeps its closing point, so the closing span is cut.\n- The band width is read at the union of both guides' knots.\n- Non-finite model facets are refused by name before any bounds.\n- The radial push-out march has a fixed step count and refuses a\n  radius that cannot advance in the float spacing.\n- The integration tests are a directory suite, tests/rotary_flow/.\n\nRefs #2824\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
